From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:16:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Windows: place iOS call-return stacks from the top of
 the FEX band

A call-return stack is 16MB and two guard pages, so on the band's 64KB
granularity it ends 64KB past a 16MB boundary. Placed bottom-up among
rpmalloc's 16MB-aligned spans, each one left a hole of nearly 16MB that
no span could use, and each emulator thread took about 64MB of the 16GB
band instead of 50 (its two spans, the stack and a 2MB L1 cache). They
are now reserved with MEM_TOP_DOWN, so they pack next to each other at
the band's top while the spans fill it from the bottom. Wine accepts
MEM_TOP_DOWN together with address requirements; Windows does not, which
is why FEXCore's own band allocations leave it out.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-28-fex-band.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 Source/Windows/Common/CallRetStack.h | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/CallRetStack.h b/Source/Windows/Common/CallRetStack.h
index 2b1ae18..8d15f86 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/CallRetStack.h
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/CallRetStack.h
@@ -114,7 +114,15 @@ bool InitializeThread(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread) {
         LogMan::Msg::EFmt("[callret] INJECTED reserve failure on call #{} -- taking the real "
                           "containment path", ThisCall);
       } else if (ios_fex_band_base) {
-      CallRetStackAlloc = ::VirtualAlloc2(nullptr, nullptr, CallRetStackAllocSize, MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_NOACCESS, &AddrParam, 1);
+      /* Playport: from the top of the band down. The stack is 16MB and two
+       * guard pages, so on the band's 64KB granularity it ends 64KB past a
+       * 16MB boundary; placed bottom-up among rpmalloc's 16MB-aligned spans,
+       * each one left a hole of nearly 16MB that no span could use, and a
+       * thread cost about 64MB of the band instead of 50. Packed at the top
+       * they sit next to each other. Wine takes MEM_TOP_DOWN together with
+       * address requirements (Windows does not). */
+      CallRetStackAlloc = ::VirtualAlloc2(nullptr, nullptr, CallRetStackAllocSize, MEM_RESERVE | MEM_TOP_DOWN, PAGE_NOACCESS,
+                                          &AddrParam, 1);
     }
   }
   /* ml706: NO unconstrained fallback here. Each 16-byte frame holds a HOST
